  "doc.title": "How Nginx Handles Ten Thousand Connections · A Hands-on Essay",
  "doc.desc": "A dozen lines of nginx.conf launch a web server, and moments later ten thousand browsers hold open keep-alive sockets against it. Following Nginx 1.28.0 stable internals and algorithms, this essay walks through the C10K memory cliff, Master-Worker zero-downtime hot reloads, the epoll event loop, the 11-phase HTTP state machine and location precedence, ngx_pool_t bump allocation, Smooth Weighted Round-Robin (SWRR), limit_req leaky-bucket pacing, red-black timer trees, sendfile zero-copy vs proxy_buffering, and November 2026 frontiers in HTTP/3 QUIC, io_uring, and Pingora / Envoy. Nine interactive models and nine schematic diagrams run the same underlying rules directly in the page.",
  "nav.back": "← Knowledge index",
