  "ch5.limit": "The model leaves out: Nginx buffer recycling across Keep-Alive requests, the shared-memory slab allocator (`ngx_slab_pool_t`) used by `limit_req` in Chapter 7, and statistical tail waste distributions under mixed header lengths.",
  "ch6.title": "Smooth Weighted Round-Robin: why `{5, 1, 1}` never hammers A five times in a row",
  "toc.ch6": "Smooth Weighted Round-Robin (SWRR)",
  "ch6.law": "Naive weighted round-robin bursts a weight-5 backend five times in a row before moving on; `ngx_http_upstream_get_peer` adds `effective_weight` every turn and subtracts total weight from the winner, interleaving `{5, 1, 1}` into `A, A, B, A, C, A, A`.",
  "ch6.p1": "Suppose three upstreams carry weights `A = 5`, `B = 1`, `C = 1` (sum = 7). Expanding them sequentially as `[A, A, A, A, A, B, C]` achieves the right 5:1:1 average, yet blasts A with `5` consecutive requests at the start of every cycle while B and C sit idle and then get hit back-to-back.",
  "ch6.p2": "In `src/http/ngx_http_upstream_round_robin.c`, Nginx keeps a dynamic `current_weight` (starting at 0) and a recovery `effective_weight` (normally equal to static `weight`) on each peer. On every incoming request:",
  "ch6.s1": "Add `effective_weight` to every peer's `current_weight`, summing the active `total`;",
  "ch6.s2": "Pick the peer with the <strong>highest</strong> `current_weight`;",
  "ch6.s3": "Subtract `total` from the <strong>winner's</strong> `current_weight`.",
  "ch6.p3": "That single subtraction enforces an exact zero-sum invariant: <strong>the sum of all peers' `current_weight` values equals 0 after every step</strong>, guaranteeing that after one 7-request period the vector returns identically to `[0, 0, 0]`. For `{5, 1, 1}`, Nginx emits `A, A, B, A, C, A, A`, dropping A's maximum consecutive burst from `5` down to `2`. And if A suffers a transient error, Nginx lowers `effective_weight` and ramps it back by +1 per round (`if (effective_weight &lt; weight) effective_weight++`) so a newly recovered node is never slammed with full weight on its very first millisecond back.",
  "dg.swrr.cap": "Figure 6. Full 7-step SWRR sequence for {A:5, B:1, C:1} and the zero-sum current_weight invariant.",
  "dg.swrr.aria": "Diagram: seven colored blocks A, A, B, A, C, A, A across the top, with step formulas and zero-sum current_weight invariant below",
  "dg.swrr.head": "7-step period for {A:5, B:1, C:1} (total = 7)",
  "dg.swrr.r1": "cw += eff; pick max; winner cw -= 7",
  "dg.swrr.r2": "Max consecutive hits on A drop from 5 to 2",
  "dg.swrr.inv1": "Invariant: sum(current_weight) ≡ 0",
  "dg.swrr.inv2": "Step 7 ends cleanly back at [0, 0, 0]",
