  "ch7.say.zero_burst": "<em>Strict pacing (burst = 0)</em>: after request #1 passes immediately, every arrival faster than {rate} r/s gets 503 ({rej} dropped) with zero burst tolerance.",
  "ch7.say.queued": "<em>Traffic shaping (no nodelay)</em>: {del} burst requests queue smoothly up to <em>{wait} ms</em> before forwarding, while {rej} requests above burst receive 503.",
  "ch7.say.nodelay": "<em>Instant burst (nodelay)</em>: the first <em>{imm}</em> requests pass with zero added sleep while filling the bucket; the remaining {rej} overflow requests still return 503.",
  "ch7.say.clean": "At {rate} r/s and burst={burst}, all {spike} requests pass immediately with zero queueing or drops.",
  "ch7.limit": "The model leaves out: `delay N` partial-nodelay thresholds, shared-memory exhaustion LRU pruning (`ngx_http_limit_req_expire`), and multi-key IP vs route zone splits.",
  "ch8.title": "Red-black tree timers: watching 10,000 timeouts through one `epoll_wait` argument",
  "toc.ch8": "Red-black timers & lazy delay",
  "ch8.law": "Nginx spawns no timer threads and never scans ten thousand sockets for timeouts. Every read, write, and keep-alive deadline enters a worker-local red-black tree, so each `epoll_wait` sleeps for the exact time remaining until the leftmost node expires.",
  "ch8.p1": "Tracking 60-second Keep-Alive and 30-second read deadlines across 10,000 sockets via a periodic array scan wastes `O(N)` work per second. In `src/event/ngx_event_timer.h` and `src/core/ngx_rbtree.c`, each worker owns one lock-free `ngx_event_timer_rbtree`:",
  "ch8.s1": "<strong>Leftmost node sets `epoll_wait` timeout</strong>: `ngx_event_find_timer()` walks left children to the minimum timestamp and passes `min_key - now` directly as the millisecond timeout to `epoll_wait`. At default (`53` ms remaining), the kernel wakes at `53` ms unless an earlier packet arrives.",
  "ch8.s2": "<strong>Wake and pop expired nodes in `O(expired)`</strong>: After `epoll_wait` returns, Nginx repeatedly pops leftmost nodes whose key `&lt;= now`, flagging `ev-&gt;timedout = 1` until the new leftmost node lies in the future.",
  "ch8.s3": "<strong>300 ms lazy timer updates (`NGX_TIMER_LAZY_DELAY`)</strong>: Reseating a node in a red-black tree on every TCP segment burns rotations unnecessarily. Nginx skips deleting and reinserting an active event's timer whenever `|new_key - old_key| &lt; 300 ms`, eliminating `85%` of tree rotations in our active-packet test while guaranteeing worst-case depth `&lt;= 2 × log2(N + 1)`—at most `26` levels even for 10,000 simultaneous timers.",
  "dg.rbtree.cap": "Figure 8. ngx_event_timer_rbtree: the leftmost minimum node (gold) sets epoll_wait's sleep limit, while 300 ms lazy updates skip frequent re-insertions.",
  "dg.rbtree.aria": "Diagram: 7-node red-black tree with leftmost gold node 355 pointing to epoll_wait timeout and bottom note on 300 ms lazy delay skipping tree updates",
  "dg.rbtree.min": "Leftmost node sets sleep limit",
  "dg.rbtree.t1": "epoll_wait(..., 355 - now)",
  "dg.rbtree.t2": "Skip delete+insert if |new - old| < 300 ms",
